@startuml AircraftManagement-SD-Unicorns
autonumber
title GET /api/v2/unicorns — a pure query on the projection AIRCRAFT_MOOD
participant ": AircraftProjection" as P <<projection>>
database "AIRCRAFT_MOOD" as T <<read model>>
actor "Client / Postman" as C
participant ": UnicornsController" as Ctrl
participant ": AircraftMoodQueryService" as Q <<query>>

== write side → projection (on every replica, when an event arrives) ==
P -> P : AircraftRegistered / AircraftStatusChanged
P -> T : upsert (registration, model, operationalStatus,\nmood = moodOf(status), timestamp = now)
note right of T
  AVAILABLE → HAPPY, IN_FLIGHT → BUSY,
  UNDER_MAINTENANCE → GROUNDED_AND_GRUMPY, else NEUTRAL
end note
== query side ==
C -> Ctrl : GET /api/v2/unicorns (JWT)
Ctrl -> Q : moods()
Q -> T : findAllOrdered()
Q --> Ctrl : List<AircraftMoodDTO> (source = "read-model")
Ctrl --> C : 200 [ { registration, model, operationalStatus, mood, timestamp, source } ]
note over C, T
  The Postman mock server returns the same JSON: consumers depend on the read-model contract,
  not on how it is produced, so the mock and this projection are interchangeable.
end note
@enduml
